     "url": "https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/g-s1-147822/up-first-newsletter-trump-ads-funding-campaign-rallies-ilhan-omar",
     "text": "The U.S. government continues to pay for ads promoting President Trump , even after he announced that his MAGA Inc. super PAC would take over funding. A federal judge ordered the ads to be taken down, yet they remained on air. An NPR analysis of data from AdImpact finds that nearly $22 million in taxpayer funds have been spent since the campaign began in late September. Almost $10 million of that was spent after Trump pledged on an Oct. 5 Truth Social post to fund the campaign privately. The White House has called the ads public service announcements, but a lawsuit by Common Cause and others …",
     "title": "Government spent millions on Trump ads. And, federal agents raid Ilhan Omar's home",
     "publishedAt": "2026-10-13T11:08:14.000Z",
     "fetchedAt": "2026-10-13T11:29:29.088Z",
